--Description (thinking process):
-- Goal: For every league, return exactly ONE team that has the fewest total match-wins (home + away)
--       across all seasons.  If several teams tie, choose the one with the smallest team_api_id so
--       the result is deterministic.
--
-- Steps inside the CTEs:
-- 1) wins_raw      – Each individual win, represented by (league_id, winning team_api_id).
-- 2) win_totals    – Count wins per (league, team).
-- 3) league_min    – Minimum win total observed inside each league.
-- 4) pick_one      – For leagues where several teams share that minimum, keep only the team whose
--                    team_api_id is the smallest (tie-break rule).
-- The final SELECT joins to League and Team to print readable names plus the win count.

WITH wins_raw AS (
    -- every home win
    SELECT league_id,
           home_team_api_id AS team_api_id
    FROM   Match
    WHERE  home_team_goal > away_team_goal
    UNION ALL
    -- every away win
